  "system": {
    "biography": "<p>A 1.2-meter bipedal reptile like a cross between an iguana and a monkey: green scales with coarse hair, a spiky iguana crest, large red eyes, a short tail and opposable thumbs. It lives in Caribbean tropical forests (and is rumored on Madagascar), drinks blood — goats and cattle by preference (\"goatsucker\"), isolated metahumans now and then. Its tissues look like HMHVV's, but it doesn't carry the virus.</p><p><strong>Powers:</strong> Concealment (Personal), Essence Drain, Immunity to Pathogens, Immunity to Poisons, Paralyzing Touch</p><p><strong>Weaknesses:</strong> Allergy (Sunlight, Mild), Essence Loss, Vulnerability (Fire)</p><p><em>Printed stats: B 5 · Q 4 × 4 · S 3 · C — · I 3/5 · W 6 · E 2D6 · R 5; Attacks 3L, claw or teeth. Running multiplier ×4; Perception 5. Cyberpirates p.147.</em></p><p><em>On the sheet: the sheet's running rate uses ×3 — use ×4 by hand; Charisma (printed —) counts as 1 on the sheet (the system's floor); Essence 7 is a typical roll — roll 2D6 for each chupacabras; Threat Rating 4 is this module's estimate (the average attribute), not the book's.</em></p>",
